From 0d93d73ec7634bb037aec220097f51118b071345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:35:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] UI: Add a toolkit-free headless frontend behind
 ENABLE_HEADLESS_UI

The new UI/Headless frontend is a LibWebView application without any
windowing toolkit: it only offers the engine's headless modes
(--headless=screenshot|layout-tree|text|manual) and WebDriver sessions,
and defaults to the text dump when no mode is given. It builds wherever
the engine and the helper processes build, which makes it the smallest
possible frontend for platforms that have no supported GUI toolkit.

Since a plain executable has no application bundle, the resource
copying, the install rules and the resource-root / helper-process lookup
in LibWebView now treat a non-bundle macOS build like the other Unix
platforms (share/Lagom and libexec next to the install prefix). Bundle
builds keep their existing layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
